# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data — exclude everything under data/ (raw inputs AND processed outputs).
# Written as `data/*` rather than `data/` on purpose: git will not descend into
# an excluded DIRECTORY, so `data/` would make the !data/frozen/ exception at
# the bottom of this file impossible. `data/*` excludes the same content while
# leaving the directory itself walkable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*

# Safety net: never track data file types anywhere in the repo
*.csv
*.parquet
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.zip

# Generated outputs living under data/ (redundant with data/, kept explicit)
data/**/*.png
data/**/*.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets / local config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pgpass
config.yaml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# System / editor junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/
.idea/
# any virtualenv in the working tree, however it is named
.venv*/
venv/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicitly KEEP tracked (code + project docs):
#   scripts/*.py, README.md, requirements.txt, .gitignore
# None of the patterns above match these. *.txt is scoped to data/ only,
# so requirements.txt stays tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Targeted exceptions to the rules above. The blanket `data/` and `*.csv` rules
# stay as they are; these re-include exactly two things:
#
#   data/frozen/  the four artefacts NO script can rebuild — the LLM sentence
#                 labels, the hand-coded validation template, the listed-bank
#                 sample and the RSSD<->permno crosswalk. Losing them ends the
#                 project, so they belong in version control.
#   results/      the showcase snapshot. data/processed/ is ignored and the raw
#                 inputs are not redistributable, so without this snapshot a
#                 clone shows an examiner nothing at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!data/frozen/
!data/frozen/*.csv
!data/frozen/*.md
!data/frozen/superseded/
!data/frozen/superseded/*.csv
!data/frozen/superseded/*.txt

# data/raw/fed/ — the eleven-document corpus. Hand-collected from
# federalreserve.gov and NOT rebuildable by any script (_fetch_fulltext.py only
# restores doc 1's body text), so it is as unreproducible as data/frozen/ and is
# tracked for the same reason. The PDF is pinned too: it is the primary source
# for doc 1 and the Fed's URLs move. Everything else under data/raw/ stays out.
!data/raw/
!data/raw/fed/
!data/raw/fed/*.xlsx
!data/raw/fed/*.txt
!data/raw/fed/*.pdf
data/raw/*
!data/raw/fed
data/raw/fed/~$*
!results/
!results/**
!results/**/*.csv
!results/**/*.png

# Working notes that are not part of the dissertation
docs/superseded_results_ru.md
